l3lint lints commercial card Level 2 and Level 3 payment payloads. Its rules come only from public sources, and
every rule cites the public pages it relies on. l3lint is not affiliated with or endorsed by Visa, Mastercard,
American Express, Discover or any processor or gateway named in its rules and documentation. Brand and product
names belong to their owners.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data bundled in the packages
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Each file below states its source in its own header. The files hold codes and short facts copied or transcribed
from public pages.

src/L3Lint.Core/Data/iso4217.csv
  ISO 4217 currency codes and minor units (list one: current currencies and funds), published 2026-09-17.
  Source: SIX Financial Information, the ISO 4217 maintenance agency:
  https://www.six-group.com/dam/download/financial-information/data-center/iso-currrency/lists/list-one.xml
  ISO 4217 is a standard of the International Organization for Standardization.

src/L3Lint.Adapters/Data/iso3166.csv
  ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 to alpha-2 country codes (codes only, no names), transcribed from the public list at
  https://www.iso.org/iso-3166-country-codes.html
  ISO 3166 is a standard of the International Organization for Standardization.

src/L3Lint.Rules.Amex/Pack/lists/amex-uom.csv
  2-character ANSI X12 unit-of-measure codes (data element 355) as listed on the public Mastercard Gateway page
  for Level 2 and 3 data with the American Express acquirer:
  https://developer.mastercard.com/mastercard-gateway/documentation/gateway-features/trans-enrich-data/order-and-line-item-data/level-2-and-3/level2-3-data-for-amex-acq/
  Cross-checked against https://www.stedi.com/edi/x12/element/355 and
  https://developer.cybersource.com/docs/cybs/en-us/api-fields/reference/all/so/api-fields/item-no-unit-of-measure.html
  ASC X12 is a standard of the Accredited Standards Committee X12.

src/L3Lint.Rules.Mastercard/Pack/lists/mastercard-uom.csv
  Mastercard Level 3 unit-of-measure codes as published by J.P. Morgan:
  https://developer.payments.jpmorgan.com/docs/commerce/online-payments/capabilities/online-payments/payment-methods/cards/commercialcards

src/L3Lint.Rules.Mastercard/Pack/lists/mastercard-l2-excluded-mcc.csv
src/L3Lint.Rules.Mastercard/Pack/lists/mastercard-l3-excluded-mcc.csv
src/L3Lint.Rules.Mastercard/Pack/lists/mastercard-tax-exempt-mcc.csv
src/L3Lint.Rules.Visa/Pack/lists/visa-product3-excluded-mcc.csv
src/L3Lint.Rules.Visa/Pack/lists/visa-federal-excluded-mcc.csv
  Merchant category code lists from Stripe's public payment line items guide:
  https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-line-items

src/L3Lint.Rules.Visa/Pack/lists/visa-fuel-mcc.csv
  Fuel merchant category codes from
  https://developer.paypal.com/braintree/docs/reference/general/level-2-and-3-processing/required-fields/dotnet/
  and https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-line-items

src/L3Lint.Rules.General/Pack/lists/placeholders.csv
  Placeholder description terms from the l3lint specification. The terms Visa is publicly reported to reject
  come from https://merchantcostconsulting.com/lower-credit-card-processing-fees/how-to-qualify-cedp-rates/ and
  https://verisave.com/blog/visa-level-2-sunset-cedp-data-quality

